    "decision": "revised",
    "changes": "Automated run (3 stations, 30-100 s, Mw 6.4 at 1 km) replaced. Band 10-50 s. Stations HPRZ LTZ DBHZ ERWZ RPZ DSZ with time shifts HPRZ +1 LTZ +1 DBHZ +2 ERWZ +2 RPZ +4 DSZ +2 s from a -8..+8 s grid sweep (every subset of 15 candidates at a fixed shallow depth, shifts refined by coordinate descent, own VR >= 25, >= 4 sectors). Inverted over the full 1-30 km grid (kept in depth_search and the depth figure); preferred depth FIXED at 4 km = maximum DC within 5 VR points of the VR maximum (VR 84-90 from 1.5 to 14 km, DC 99 at 4 km falling to 49 at 8 km). SMRZ KHZ CVZ THZ OXZ excluded (bad records; OXZ 10x amplitude).",
    "notes": "Mw 4.82, 240/61/159 and 341/72/31, VR 88.5, DC 99, every own VR 82-95, leave-one-out rotation 3.7 deg with the shifts kept. Strike matches the SKHASH first-motion plane 243/88/180 and USGS Mwr 4.8 (13 km); dip 61 at this depth. Azimuth gap 159 deg (all six stations lie NE-SW); adding GVZ (+3 s) closes it to 129 deg with the mechanism unchanged (243/64/164, VR 82, DC 84), INZ and IFMZ to the west only fit at own VR 30-50. Shift sweep is what made this work: the SW stations DBHZ ERWZ RPZ need +2 to +4 s and look like bad data under free cross-correlation. Predicted peak surface displacement 0.6 cm at 4 km (0.03 cm for the 16 km alternative)."
